WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.180
Ancient DNA confirms Kakao reached Eastern North America by the 11th century. This is Planetarian

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:13.380
Daily, episode 164. Researchers examined residues from the Mississippi and city of Etowa and detected

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:19.520
Kakao DNA in artifacts dated to the 11th and 12th centuries. The finding pushes back the

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.700
known timeline for Kakao consumption in Eastern North America by several hundred years.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.880
Kakao, the source of chocolate, was previously documented mainly in Mesoamerica during that era.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:37.880
The study appears in PLOS1 and relied on targeted ancient DNA recovery from ceramic vessels.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.460
Next steps include broader sampling across other Mississippi and sites to map trade routes. On a

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.860
different note, researchers define intrinsic capacity as the composite of physical, cognitive,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:56.320
sensory, and psychological reserves that determine functional aging. Longitudinal cohorts show that

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.960
declines in this measure predict disability and mortality more reliably than single biomarkers.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.220
The World Health Organization has incorporated the concept into its healthy aging framework.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.340
Clinicians can track it through simple batteries of tests rather than advanced imaging.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.560
Ongoing trials are testing interventions that preserve multiple domains simultaneously.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:23.840
Now shifting from broad aging measures to specific dietary patterns that may influence long-term

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:30.860
health outcomes. Analysis of more than 17,000 U.S. men found that higher consumption of soft drinks,

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:38.860
packaged snacks, and processed meats corresponded to 24-31% elevated prostate cancer incidents after

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:45.660
adjustment for age, smoking, and socioeconomic factors. The association held across racial and

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:51.460
ethnic groups. Mechanisms under investigation include chronic inflammation and disruptions to

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:57.020
metabolic hormone balance. The study used nationally representative dietary recall data.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:02.760
Replication in other cohorts is planned. The ultra-processed food study tracked more than

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:10.740
17,000 men and isolated at 24-31% rise in prostate cancer risk, tied to higher intake of packaged

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:16.880
snacks, cereals, and processed meats. The association survived adjustment for smoking, poverty,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.920
and race, pointing to mechanisms beyond simple calorie excess.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:26.700
Inflammation and hormone disruption are the leading biological explanations under investigation.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.480
What remains unclear is whether modest reductions in these foods produce measurable risk drops

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:38.660
within a few years. Most people assume any diet cancer link comes down to excess calories or

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:44.540
missing nutrients. In reality, ultra-processed foods appear to act through additional roots that

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:49.380
alter inflammation and hormone signaling even when total energy intake is controlled.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.800
Right now, as you digest a packaged snack, emulsifiers and additives can shift gut barrier

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.520
permeability and circulating inflammatory markers within hours. One memorable number from

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:08.320
recent U.S. data shows men in the highest intake group had 24-31% higher prostate cancer

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:14.040
incidents after standard risk-factor adjustments. The next time you reach for a ready-to-eat meal,

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.260
notice how many ingredients on the label have no direct culinary counterpart.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:23.840
Watching future trials that swap whole foods for matched ultra-processed versions will

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:29.680
clarify whether the risk signal shrinks when those additives disappear. From population-level

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:35.060
diet effects, evidence of food trade and consumption patterns appears in much earlier records.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:40.760
Yale researchers combine new computational tools with ancient DNA from museum specimens

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:46.900
to recover sequences from two previously unknown giant tortoise populations. Both lineages

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:52.080
disappeared after human arrival on the islands. The method improves recovery from highly

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:58.140
fragmented samples that standard approaches miss. The work clarifies historical biodiversity on the

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:03.860
archipelago before modern extinctions. Further application to other island systems is planned.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:10.500
From recovered ancient biomolecules, new computational approaches are recovering even more degraded

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:16.360
genetic material. A study tested machine learning models on Atlantic Ocean data and showed they

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:22.220
can flag developing disturbances several days before traditional systems detect them. The AI draws

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:28.420
on large-scale atmospheric patterns that precedes storm organization. Forecasts gain lead time

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:34.380
without replacing existing dynamical models. The approach was validated against historical storm

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:40.500
seasons. Operational testing with weather agencies is the next phase. From atmospheric prediction,

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:47.060
algorithms are optimizing another complex physical process. Engineers used an algorithm to evaluate

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:54.180
more than 100 million parameter combinations for 3D printing GR-COP-42. A copper alloy used in

00:04:54.520 --> 00:05:00.640
rocket engines. After 40 physical trials, the system located six viable settings, including one

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:06.640
at 500 watts. Lower power requirements expand the range of printers that can produce the material.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.620
The work reduces cost barriers that previously limited adoption.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:16.680
Follow-on tests will assess mechanical performance of the new prints. From machine learning in

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.440
material science, attention turns to altered gravity effects on female physiology.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:27.980
Begum-mathic and collaborators are extending earlier spaceflight data to examine how microgravity

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:34.100
and radiation interact with reproductive and endocrine systems in women. The project builds on samples

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:40.400
collected two years ago and adds new assays for hormone signaling and tissue response. Longer

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:46.160
missions increase the need for sex-specific countermeasures. Data will inform habitat design and

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:51.980
medical protocols for deep space travel. Results are expected to guide selection criteria for future

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:57.820
crews. On another front, schools that remove student phones during instructional hours recorded

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:03.580
measurable improvements in attention and test performance. High schools saw smaller or inconsistent

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:09.620
effects, suggesting developmental differences in susceptibility to distraction. The study compared

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:15.560
matched schools before and after policy changes. Teachers reported fewer behavioral interruptions

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:20.800
once devices were stored. Provincial data collection continues to assess longer-term mental

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:27.140
health outcomes. Shifting to agricultural findings, University of Queensland trials added green bin

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:32.800
compost to commercial tomato fields and measured both chemical profiles and sensory panels.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:39.060
Treated fruit scored higher in sweetness and overall aroma intensity. The effect traces to

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:44.360
increased availability of certain soil micronutrients that influence sugar and volatile production.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:49.620
Control plots without compost produce blender fruit under identical irrigation.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:54.440
Larger scale adoption could divert organic waste while raising crop value.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:07:00.680
After 20 years of fieldwork, a University of North Carolina Asheville researcher compiled the

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:06.020
initial comprehensive inventory of the island's native terrestrial reptiles in Turks and Kekos.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:12.300
The illustrated guide covers distribution, habitat preferences, and conservation status for each

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:18.000
species. Several taxa are endemic and face pressure from habitat loss and invasive predators.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:22.520
The reference supports both scientific surveys and local protection planning.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:28.620
Digital versions will allow citizen scientists to contribute sightings. Researchers warn that highly

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:34.400
pathogenic avian influenza could spill over into iconic marsupials that lack prior exposure.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:40.140
Bate delivered vaccines are under consideration as a proactive shield for vulnerable populations.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:45.660
Modeling shows transmission risk rises with longer migration routes of infected birds.

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:50.300
Field trials of oral vaccines in related species are already underway.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:54.580
Surveillance networks are expanding to detect early cases in wildlife.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:00.220
Lynch Hoping University experiments demonstrated that participants weighed envious comparisons

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:05.180
more heavily when resources were allocated by majority vote than when they chose alone.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:09.940
The effect arises because personal responsibility diffuses across the group.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.280
When votes are unlikely to be decisive, individuals focus more on relative outcomes.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.620
The finding helps explain polarization in collective resource debates.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:23.580
Follow-up work will test interventions that restore accountability.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:28.960
Before we go, keep an eye on further validation of the machine learning cyclone models

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:32.080
as they move into operational testing with weather agencies.

